WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.833
STEPHANIE WONG: The
last day of Next is here

00:00:01.833 --> 00:00:03.320
and it's all about
the community.

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:06.030
Community Day features sessions,
interactive experiences,

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:08.852
and demos for technical
practitioners, like yourself.

00:00:08.852 --> 00:00:11.310
While the live broadcast will
highlight some of my favorite

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:14.100
sessions, you can find all
of the Community Day sessions

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:17.393
available on-demand
at g.co/cloud/next.

00:00:17.393 --> 00:00:19.560
Keep in mind that you can
filter on the catalog page

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.290
by learning level, like
introductory, intermediate,

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:25.020
and advanced; track,
like AI and ML,

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:28.290
app dev, databases, or
infrastructure; job role,

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:31.230
like student, architect,
SRE, networking professional,

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.759
or security professional.

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:36.090
Now my recommendations for
the channel 1 broadcast

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.070
include a session
with Urs, our VP

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:41.160
of infrastructure, who will talk
through new developer-focused

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:42.150
announcements.

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:45.750
Don't miss this session, called
"Unleash the Innovators."

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.690
Then we're going to hop
into a spectacular DEI

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:51.090
session with one of the
founders of the internet,

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:54.630
"A conversation with Vint Cerf
and Jim Hogan on disability

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:55.530
in tech."

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:59.310
Next, go ahead and meet
the Women Techmakers team.

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:01.710
And then join the
learning and certification

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:03.420
Q&amp;A with our experts.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.910
And check out "Making
infrastructure invisible

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:07.470
for application
developers," where

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:10.260
you can discover how storage
can take care of failover

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:13.560
and disaster recovery with
automated data replication

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.200
and how networking can remove
the complexity of traffic

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.120
management as traffic grows.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.940
"Building better partnerships
with open source communities"

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.710
will be a session
with the teams who

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:25.410
contributed to open source
projects this past year,

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:28.650
like Tensorflow,
Kubernetes, and Apache Beam,

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:31.630
and they even helped with
COVID-19 response efforts.

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:33.840
I also want to highlight
"Designing and building

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.750
serverless solutions," which
will feature my teammates,

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:39.210
developer advocates
for a group discussion

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:42.090
on Cloud Run, Cloud
Functions, and App Engine.

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:44.490
So you are going to learn
what workloads are best suited

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:46.830
for serverless and
some tips and tricks.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.900
Channel 2 of the broadcast
will cover sessions

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:51.180
on ML and Google
Developer Community

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:54.090
gatherings for both
North America and APAC.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.280
And channel 3 is all
about hands-on labs

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:59.340
for GKE Autopilot, ETL
processing with Dataflow,

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:01.380
Vertex AI, and security.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:03.930
So I hope you enjoy our
final day three of Next.

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:06.600
And remember, connect on
social with the hashtag

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.699
#GoogleCloudNext, and reach
out to me @stephr_wong.

